toastsaver (1.8.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Picker: tap a picture to watch that saver full screen; nothing changes.
    Tap its heart to keep it in your screensaver. One heart plays that
    saver, several take turns, and the last heart stays. A bar under the
    tiles says what will play. This replaces SURPRISE ME! and the TRY IT!
    band; existing settings carry over as hearts.
  * Watching a saver from the picker holds off the idle watcher, so the
    kept saver no longer starts over the top of it.
  * Picker: tiles no longer clip: frames and rings are even all round and
    stay clear of the titles.
  * Settings: rows are grouped, and BOOKS: EACH PAGE sets how long each
    poem page stays up.
  * Rainbow: astronaut pugs in glass helmets drift through space.

 -- piyh <10518137+piyh@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0000

toastsaver (1.7.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * New CITY saver: a sunny pixel-art street with towers, shops and houses.
    People stroll, look at their phones, wear very cool sunglasses, ride
    bikes and walk dogs (one corgi has a very big butt); cats sit on
    fences, awnings and roofs; pigeons scatter; cars and a bus stop at the
    traffic light; chimneys smoke and flocks of birds cross the sky.
  * Picker: every tile has a glassy TRY IT! band over the bottom of its
    picture that plays just that saver, without changing the choice or the
    SURPRISE mix, so a quick look at one saver needs no deselecting. Each
    saver's name is now a title above its picture, and the picture and the
    band light up separately on hover. The big TRY IT! button is gone.
  * Books: a wider, larger open book with the poem set smaller, several
    stanzas to a page, and the clock keeps off the open book. "I Love
    Little Pussy" replaces The Owl and the Pussy-Cat.
  * New BOOK_PAGE_SECONDS setting: how long each page of a poem stays up.

 -- piyh <10518137+piyh@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000

toastsaver (1.6.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Volcano: the finale throws the cone apart. Thin rock near the summit
    flies fast as small fragments, the thick base shrugs outward as slow
    slabs, and the crater settles into a partly filled bowl.
  * Volcano: rock has real heat. It flows between touching rock, quenches
    fast in the sea and slowly in air; small debris goes dark at once while
    big lumps keep a glowing core, in the air and under water alike.
  * Volcano: new channels bend toward rock still warm from old ones, sealed
    channels stay in the cone as dark red dikes, and the magma chamber stays
    full, glowing and churning harder as its pressure builds.
  * Volcano: the whale dives and swims away from eruptions and rides the
    swell smoothly instead of every ripple.
  * Windowed mode: B sets off the volcano's finale now, F fast-forwards to
    it and drops back to normal speed when it starts, and the speed goes up
    to 512x (as fast as the computer can run it).
  * Books: each book shows a real public-domain rhyme or poem with its
    title, in order from a random start. Pages turn over like paper, every
    story keeps its own book, and there are six new stories and pictures.
  * Rainbow: a unicorn gallops across the sky every few minutes (or on E),
    and the Waffle Cat is livelier.

 -- piyh <10518137+piyh@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000

toastsaver (1.5.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fixes the screensaver no longer starting after changing a time in
    Settings: with a gamepad plugged in, the restarted idle watcher could
    give up while the old one was still shutting down.
  * The idle watcher keeps a log (~/.local/state/toastsaver/idle.log) of
    when it starts and stops and why; toastsaver-idle --check shows the end.
  * The clock keeps clear of numbers on screen: the dice, their total and
    the tallies flying to the chalkboard.

